        &lt;description&gt;In this story, you will simulate the creation of a basic application service using Service Mapping. You will manually create Calculated Application Service named “CRM Platform Service” and populate it with key infrastructure components:&amp;#13;
&amp;#13;
A Load Balancer (LB-CRM)&amp;#13;
&amp;#13;
A Web Server (CRM Web Server)&amp;#13;
&amp;#13;
An Application Server (CRM App Server)&amp;#13;
&amp;#13;
A Database (CRM DB Server)&amp;#13;
&amp;#13;
You will define their relationships to show how traffic flows from users to the back-end database through the application. Once the structure is complete, you’ll use Service Mapping to generate the service topology map. The map should visually represent dependencies and paths between these CIs.&amp;#13;
&amp;#13;
This exercise simulates a real-world scenario where service maps are used to understand impact and plan changes.&amp;#13;
&amp;#13;
Tip: Use a Wizard for creation of new Application Service, For relationship types use Suggested Relationships in CI Class Manager for your Application Service&lt;/description&gt;
